# #PAGE — workspace and delivery contract

Load this module before creating or updating a Page or treating a Page as a
project destination.

## PAGE-001 — Meaning

A `#PAGE` is a configured, human-readable workspace and delivery surface in markdown format. It
may display project status, source links, `#FACT` records, tables, gaps, and
artifact links. It is not automatically a durable database, complete
transcript, machine-readable source of truth, or permission grant.

## PAGE-002 — Required configuration

Record the Page ID or destination, account/workspace, owner, intended audience,
read/write authorization, sensitivity, project ID, source artifacts, update
cadence, and completion-state policy. If any material field is unknown, block
only the action that depends on it.

## PAGE-003 — Updates

Read the latest Page before editing and preserve human changes. Update from the
controlled project records, retain stable IDs, distinguish draft and complete
material, and link complete machine-readable artifacts rather than hiding
omitted rows behind a summary table.

Do not display a completion notice until acceptance tests pass. Do not treat a
successful upload as proof that a link was added, resolves, or has the intended
audience.

## PAGE-004 — Delivery verification

After an update, verify the returned reference, access scope, visible content,
artifact links, dates/versions, stable IDs, and readback. Record a publication
receipt containing the Page/file ID, URL, content hash or version when
available, row counts where applicable, access result, and verification time.

